\f1\fs22 While both Ajent Jones and Gerry Hardman were PAPER agents, the former knew nothing about the latter, because the upper echelons of institutional stupidity deemed, on the basis of need-to-know, there was no need for Agent Jones to know Gerry Hardman was a fellow agent. And so Agent Jones didn\'92t know. Had it been deemed he did need to know, then he would have known, and would have no need to know what to do about Gerry, since he would already know what to about Gerry, which would be nothing, because he would know. As it was, Agent Jones didn\'92t know what any sane person would know he needed to know, given the circumstances.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones became the good kind of angry again, the kind he could manage. And now he new he was channelling an inner wisdom as well. And with a newfound lack of self criticism he wrote 
\f2\i Gerry Hardman
\f1\i0  over and over in ever-blacker letters. He broke point after pencil point and tossed them at the wall. He even cracked one in half. Running low, he shortened his scribblings to repeating:\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>G. Hardman
\f1\i0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>which in the throes of some kind frothing demon possession transformed into iterations of:\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\

\f2\i <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>G hard man\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\i0 \cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Then Agent Jones stopped as if afflicted with paralysis. He took a long cathartic breath. His eyes watered.  His pencil poised millimetres above the pad. Then, with eyes afire, he wrote:\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Jihad man
